# Bytecode from this repository's own scripts/ directory.
#
# Every project gets `scripts/*.py`, whatever its language: the generators and the
# hook entry points. Two of those hooks import a sibling module -- attribution_guard
# reads attribution_patterns, commit-msg-rewrite reads close_keywords -- and an import
# writes bytecode next to the module. So the first commit in a fresh Rust, Go or
# TypeScript repository left `scripts/__pycache__/` untracked and unignored, and a
# `git add -A` committed it. The Python layer ignores this too; a project with no
# Python layer needs it just as much.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
